            },
            {
                "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                "word": "ungreen",
                "pos": "verb",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "8aff1302-7cfa-4640-965f-e38ff896c9c7",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "tags": [
                            "present",
                            "singular",
                            "third-person"
                        ],
                        "form": "ungreens"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "fa3c6e93-7056-4bc4-92e6-ea846d014053",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "ungreening"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "76484ccb-1fad-4719-aa39-199e941520d5",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "ungreened"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "bd2caef5-37bc-47be-81e1-bfd8cd0584b4",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "ungreened"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79db648f-4858-388f-8da5-3f139628f989",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To expose to air after dyeing in indigo so that the greenish color fades away."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c32dfa12-27d4-44e9-a15b-2cfbc5fd8a34",
                                "sense_id": "79db648f-4858-388f-8da5-3f139628f989",
                                "text": "When necessary to air and ungreen, by drawing the pulley the frame rises, and the cloth drains into the vat."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed008399-7c87-40ae-84da-cb9c3acb6ef4",
                                "sense_id": "79db648f-4858-388f-8da5-3f139628f989",
                                "text": "After the expiration of this time, suspend a second lock of wool for ten or fifteen minutes in the Vat; when it comes out, it should be of a deeper shade, and more like a grass green than the first lock was: it will take a little over five minutes to ungreen it, when it will assume almost a Middle Blue, with a slight tinge of Green, after it has been exposed to the air for half an hour."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8957211e-55d2-4a94-8e42-e1f5073ad51e",
                                "sense_id": "79db648f-4858-388f-8da5-3f139628f989",
                                "text": "After each immersion the champignon is lifted out of the vat, and the fabrics are left to ungreen themselves by contact with the air. (It must be observed that, although soluble indigo is called white, because it is without color when carefully prepared in the laboratory, the goods, when first taken from the ordinary vat, are of a green color.)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c0f9cb7e-0f37-3314-b2be-91dc1a7831be",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make or become familiar with and adept in handling a new environment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa745a04-70da-40d7-b64e-66f1150610c9",
                                "sense_id": "c0f9cb7e-0f37-3314-b2be-91dc1a7831be",
                                "text": "Freshmen are called greens, and a ceremony was (and perhaps is) used in ungreening them, and admitting them to their full academical privileges."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb73f54b-b97b-43c5-9fa1-ccbe5e816f5a",
                                "sense_id": "c0f9cb7e-0f37-3314-b2be-91dc1a7831be",
                                "text": "The period of “ungreening” is closed by a solemn meeting where the novitiates are addressed by the president of the Corporation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba232089-e826-43e4-8875-76ba35af0326",
                                "sense_id": "c0f9cb7e-0f37-3314-b2be-91dc1a7831be",
                                "text": "Then the short period of orientation ( “sich oisgreenen\" ) to ungreen the greenhorn; to look up landsleit and relatives; to learn a few words of English; to familiarize oneself with the new surroundings and environment;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e1e46e3-effe-4689-a2d0-78136ab54a47",
                                "sense_id": "c0f9cb7e-0f37-3314-b2be-91dc1a7831be",
                                "text": "At the turn of the century Yiddish audiences were still greenhorns fighting to \"ungreen\" themselves ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "141db982-0a93-366c-87e4-147074b5208e",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To change from green to some other color, as occurs with leaves in the autumn."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "62e550a0-60d4-4739-bb5f-1ec54c84a2a4",
                                "sense_id": "141db982-0a93-366c-87e4-147074b5208e",
                                "text": "Harvests are congratulated She is pleased with the sight, Sweet hard apples and Small ungreening leaves."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "da16b164-e808-405b-a2cd-a9e0ae2f6ef5",
                                "sense_id": "141db982-0a93-366c-87e4-147074b5208e",
                                "text": "We watched the ungreening of the trees as they put on their fall wardrobes of bright colors."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9728865d-be21-4837-9195-29359d4e972f",
                                "sense_id": "141db982-0a93-366c-87e4-147074b5208e",
                                "text": "For these two weeks every August, the katydid chorus overlaps the buntings' song while the efts crawl up the trail along the river and the breakdown of chlorophyll begins to ungreen the leaves."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cf88b7b-46b0-38e9-a663-1ce55fea47fc",
                        "entry_id": "3ba43198-4b36-38d9-be59-089d2968921a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To urbanize or become less environmentally friendly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "17d5c6ce-80cd-4211-a193-76a846f53dd1",
                                "sense_id": "1cf88b7b-46b0-38e9-a663-1ce55fea47fc",
                                "text": "John Robinson, in “Highways and Our Environment,\" complains that the highway system not only has disfigured our countryside by slapping down acres of concrete that threatens to ungreen America, but also carries an increasing number of cars that further befoul the environment by thrusting more pollutants into the air."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7abe285-ad45-478b-b2de-1ac932bf3fd5",
                                "sense_id": "1cf88b7b-46b0-38e9-a663-1ce55fea47fc",
                                "text": "“Socioeconomic threshold” refers to a combination of societal and economic acceptable levels of the six factors to measure purpose accomplishment—in effect, how much “ungreening” would be tolerated by the citizenry before there was a demand for action."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33979489-b61c-45f4-8cd9-3a3047e32a25",
                                "sense_id": "1cf88b7b-46b0-38e9-a663-1ce55fea47fc",
                                "text": "The ungreening world insistently intrudes as natural fact, as cultural locus, and – so pastoral reminds us – as literary tradition."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "80fc658b-4add-4d0c-9703-0effcb5ad944",
                                "sense_id": "1cf88b7b-46b0-38e9-a663-1ce55fea47fc",
                                "text": "According to Munters, the 'ungreening' of local political power positions was 20 to 30 years behind the 'ungreening' of the rural community population."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
